<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila sechellia Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm (Holocene, detail scale s0) (Drosophila sechellia)",
        "Drosophila sechellia Turing wavelength at 1.5 µm (Holocene, detail scale s0) faithfully reproduces Drosophila sechellia morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila sechellia specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila sechellia" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That 1.5 µm was measured as a granule spacing in D. sechellia.",
        "does_not_claim: That Morinda octanoic-acid resistance sets k_c.",
        "does_not_claim: That a second assessor scored this pass.",
        "does_not_claim: The 88 µm cellular wavelength already modelled in slot 2711.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Critical-shell wavelength distinct from the brightest Fourier bin; zoomed dispersion lobe; ablation annotation clear of the tick labels.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Near-onset Jacobians with analytical wavelengths 1.921, 1.680 and 1.500 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Chenoweth & Blows 2005: D. serrata signal traits are under mutual sexual selection.",
        "reported_in_source: Jeong 2008: D. santomea lost abdominal pigment via a tan enhancer.",
        "reported_in_source: McGregor 2007 and Sucena & Stern 2000: D. sechellia larval trichome loss is cis-regulatory at shavenbaby.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: k_c from the dispersion relation, and instability only when diffusivities differ.",
        "transfer_boundary: Shoup 1966 is D. melanogaster ultrastructure, used only as a scale class.",
        "transfer_boundary: The CC-BY image is a nucleic-acid stain of an ovary, not an ocellar pigment-granule micrograph." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila sechellia (Seychelles Morinda-Specialist Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-sechellia-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_sechellia_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila sechellia; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: k_c from the dispersion relation, and instability only when diffusivities differ. | McGregor 2007 and Sucena & Stern 2000: D. sechellia larval trichome loss is cis-regulatory at shavenbaby. | Jeong 2008: D. santomea lost abdominal pigment via a tan enhancer. | Chenoweth & Blows 2005: D. serrata signal traits are under mutual sexual selection.; reconstructed_in_script: Near-onset Jacobians with analytical wavelengths 1.921, 1.680 and 1.500 µm. | Critical-shell wavelength distinct from the brightest Fourier bin; zoomed dispersion lobe; ablation annotation clear of the tick labels.; transfer_boundary: The CC-BY image is a nucleic-acid stain of an ovary, not an ocellar pigment-granule micrograph. | Shoup 1966 is D. melanogaster ultrastructure, used only as a scale class.; does_not_claim: That 1.5 µm was measured as a granule spacing in D. sechellia. | That Morinda octanoic-acid resistance sets k_c. | The 88 µm cellular wavelength already modelled in slot 2711. | That a second assessor scored this pass.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
